---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Editorial scope, interactive explainers, and technical notes behind Signal & Substrate."
>
  <section class="about-page">
    <nav class="back-nav mono" aria-label="Return to index">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Index</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="page-meta mono">colophon &amp; scope</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">About Signal &amp; Substrate</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Signal &amp; Substrate</strong> is an independent technical notebook
        focused on the intersection of AI safety, machine learning mechanics, and
        the data engineering systems that sustain both.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial Scope</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>AI Safety</strong> — Mechanistic interpretability, representation
          monitoring, linear probes, and evaluation failure modes under distribution
          shift.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Machine Learning</strong> — Optimization dynamics, sampling
          geometry, quantization tradeoffs, and empirical ablations stripped of
          marketing noise.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data Engineering</strong> — Deterministic backfills, storage
          layouts, watermark contracts, and pipeline invariants that survive
          schema evolution.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Interactive Explainers</h2>
      <p>
        Entries marked <span class="mono">[interactive]</span> in the index open
        self-contained browser simulations built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and
        JavaScript. Each interactive piece lives outside the main Markdown
        pipeline so numerical experiments can run directly in the browser without
        bundle bloat.
      </p>

      <h2>Format &amp; Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        Built statically with Astro Content Collections and plain scoped CSS. Zero
        third-party UI frameworks, zero client-side analytics, and zero decorative
        images. Subscribe via <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> or inspect the static
        source on
        <a
          href="https://github.com/signalsubstrate"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .back-nav {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-link);
  }

  .page-header {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .page-meta {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-article-title);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
</style>
